window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["st-01.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">شرح الدليل الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> إذا المقود ثقيل افحص الجهد أولاً ثم العقل.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">C = الهيكل والحساسات: 11</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 16</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">27 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c15c1-00 eps mechanical performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C15C1-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">EPS MECHANICAL PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. Vehicle speed above 30 km/h (19 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects high friction in the steering system when requesting a motor torque change and rotor positioning is not responding within two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS is disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SUSPENSION DAMAGE OR MECHANICAL FAILURE</li><li>STEERING GEAR IMPROPERLY INSTALLED, DAMAGED OR MECHANICAL FAILURE</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>INSPECT THE FRONT SUSPENSION FOR DAMAGE OR MECHANICAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Visually inspect the Front Suspension for binding, damage or mechanical failure. Refer to WHEEL ALIGNMENT, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT THE STEERING GEAR FOR INCORRECT INSTALLATION, DAMAGE OR MECHANICAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Pay particular attention to the inner tie rod boots for damage.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Visually inspect the Steering Gear for Improper installation, damage or mechanical failure. Refer to GEAR, INSTALLATION .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at road speeds above 30 k/mh (19 mph) and evaluate return effort of power steering.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Park the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there excessive return effort in the power steering or is the DTC active at this time?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c15db-00 eps disabled\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C15DB-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">EPS DISABLED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DTC C15C1-00 or DTC C2217-00 has set multiple times.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS is disabled. Power Steering assist is turned off on the next key cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If DTC C15C1-00 or C2217-00 are present, refer to the diagnostics for these DTCs before continuing with this diagnostic procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the ambient temperature of the vehicle is above -40°C (-40°F)</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read and record the Environmental Data to help identify the conditions in which the DTC was set.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle at speeds above 30 k/mh (19 mph).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Park the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring harness and electrical connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2129-16 battery voltage circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2129-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module supply voltage below 10.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS Module supply voltage below 10.0 volts: Power Steering assist reduced. EPS lamp not illuminated.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS Module supply voltage below 9.0 volts: No Power Steering assist. EPS lamp illuminated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>(A951) B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>(Z906) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the PCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any Charging System or related voltage DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs while turning the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(A951) B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Wiggle test the wiring harness and electrical connectors while testing the circuit.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A951) Fused B+ circuit at the EPS C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A951) Fused B+ circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>(Z906) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Wiggle test the wiring harness and electrical connectors while testing the circuit.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a test light connected to B+ check (Z906) Ground circuit at the EPS Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (Z906) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2129-17 battery voltage circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2129-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects the battery voltage has increased above 16.5 volts for more than 1 second.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS is disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the PCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Charging System or related voltage DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate Charging System DTC diagnostic procedures before continuing with this test. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c212a-84 system voltage signal below allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C212A-84</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE SIGNAL BELOW ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أقل من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module receives a message over the CAN bus that battery voltage has decreased below 10.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module operates correctly and stores the DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM VOLTAGE LOW</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the PCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any Charging System or related voltage DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">properly.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c212a-85 system voltage signal above allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C212A-85</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE SIGNAL ABOVE ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أعلى من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module receives a message over the CAN bus that battery voltage has increased above 16.0 volts for more than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module operates correctly and stores the DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</li><li>CHARGING SYSTEM VOLTAGE HIGH</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the PCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Are there any Charging System or related voltage DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the appropriate Charging System DTC diagnostic procedures before continuing with this test. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Battery is in good condition.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the AGM Battery Tester, test the Battery before continuing. (special tool #GR8-1220KIT- CHRY, AGM Battery Tester/Charger Station)</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Does the Battery pass the load test for this specific application?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Battery in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BATTERY, REMOVAL .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2206-00 vehicle configuration mismatch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2206-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE CONFIGURATION MISMATCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No under voltage DTCs.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Vehicle type is not identified or incorrectly identified.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS is disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) NOT CONFIGURED</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Powertrain Control Module (PCM), Vehicle Identification Number (VIN), or Communication DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electric Power Steering (EPS) DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) FOR PROPER CONFIGURATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool perform the BCM Restore Vehicle Configuration.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does this DTC reset?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test Complete.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c220d-00 electrical powered hydraulic steering module internal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C220D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ELECTRICAL POWERED HYDRAULIC STEERING MODULE INTERNAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module&#x27;s power supply is interrupted during the current ignition cycle, this DTC will become active. On the next ignition key cycle, this DTC&#x27;s status will remain active during this time, however the EPS Module will operate normally. The DTC status will go to stored on the next key cycle if the EPS Module was inactive for five seconds.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module checks to see if the last shutdown occurred correctly.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System operating normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) OR CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>RELATED DTCS</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) OR COMMUNICATION</li><li>RELATED DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read and record Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Park the vehicle on level ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Tun the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring harness and electrical connectors.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR CHARGING SYSTEM OR RELATED DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the PCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any Charging System or related voltage DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) OR COMMUNICATION RELATED DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any BCM or Communication related DTCs active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedures before continuing with this test. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2210-00 ecu overtemperature\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2210-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU OVERTEMPERATURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module is sensing steering system temperature is above 130°C (266°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has lost partial or full assist.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>STEERING GEAR MECHANICAL FAILURE</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>INSPECT THE STEERING GEAR FOR INCORRECT INSTALLATION, DAMAGE OR MECHANICAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check with customer for unusual driving terrain (e.g. mud, snow, ice) or aggressive driving maneuvers at the time of set condition.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Turn the ignition off.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Visually inspect the Steering Gear for Improper installation, damage or mechanical failure. Refer to GEAR, INSTALLATION .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Let the vehicle sit for 30 minutes before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electric Power Steering (EPS) DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the steering wheel from stop to stop four to five times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring harness and electrical connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2217-00 electric power steering module internal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2217-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ELECTRIC POWER STEERING MODULE INTERNAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an internal fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has lost partial or full assist.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is disconnected and the ignition is cycled three times, the EPS Module will be disabled permanently and the steering gear must be replaced.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electric Power Steering (EPS) DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2219-00 ecu unable to configure/configuration not learned\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2219-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU UNABLE TO CONFIGURE/CONFIGURATION NOT LEARNED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If any of the learned Vehicle Configuration data from the CAN Bus has changed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS system has reduced power steering assist.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE NOT CONFIGURED</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If multiple DTCs are present, inspect the wiring and harness connector at the EPS Assembly.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module was replaced, verify that the correct EPS Assembly was installed on the vehicle.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Lost Communication DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTC diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CONFIGURATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, verify that the BCM has been configured.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Was the BCM configured correctly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not disconnect the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector and make sure it is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the EPS Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the EPS Module harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with service information. .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the BCM harness connectors. Be certain that the harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with service information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0002-00 can c bus off performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0002-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Perform the SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C procedure. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0100-00 lost communication with ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0100-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ECM/PCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0101-00 lost communication with tcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0101-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH TCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع TCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0121-00 lost communication with anti-lock brake system (abs) control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0121-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MODULE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0155-00 lost communication with cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0155-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0212-00 lost communication with scm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0212-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH SCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع SCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0401-00 implausible data received from ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0401-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ECM/PCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-00-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any PCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN C BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN C BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS Verification Test. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0402-00 implausible data received from tcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0402-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM TCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من TCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-00-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ABS INTERMITTENT CONDITION TEST. Refer to ABS INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any TCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN C BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN C BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Transmission Control Module (TCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS Verification Test. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0415-00 implausible data received from abs\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0415-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ABS</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ABS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE DTCS</li><li>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ABS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any ABS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN C BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN C BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Anti-lock</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Brake System (ABS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the EPS Verification Test. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0422-00 implausible data received from body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0422-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Body Control Module (BCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CAN BUS DTCS ARE PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any BCM CAN BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedures. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN C BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN C BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Body Control Module (BCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS Verification Test. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1215-00 lost communication with forward facing camera\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1215-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1415-00 implausible/missing vehicle configuration data\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1415-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE/MISSING VEHICLE CONFIGURATION DATA</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-88-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module receives incorrect vehicle configuration information from the Body Control Module (BCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN BUS DTCS SET IN BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CAN BUS DTCS SET IN BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Verify that the BCM has the correct vehicle configuration before</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">proceeding with this test step.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the BCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any active CAN Bus DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the EPS Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1447-00 implausible data received from scm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1447-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM SCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من SCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No U0002-00-CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An error message has been received over the CAN C bus from the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System is operating at 50 percent efficiency. Park assist not functioning.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE DTCS</li><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM) DTCS</li><li>ELECTRONIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any Instrument Cluster DTCs before proceeding with this diagnostic procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR DTCS IN THE SCCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in the SCCM.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the SCM reporting any DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CAN C BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any CAN C BUS DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, STEERING COLUMN CONTROL (SCCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS Verification Test. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u148d-00 implausible data received from forward facing camera\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U148D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. One valid CAN message received at least once. No CAN C Bus Off Performance DTC present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects an incorrect CAN message from the Forward Facing Camera Module (FFCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS System has reduced or degraded assist under some conditions.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE CAN BUS DTCS</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS</li><li>FORWARD FACING CAMERA MODULE (FFCM) DTCS</li><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li><li>FORWARD FACING CAMERA MODULE (FFCM) DTCS</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs and record on the vehicle repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the EPS DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition from off to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Are there any BCM CAN Bus DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR FORWARD FACING CAMERA MODULE (FFCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the FFCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any FFCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other modules reporting implausible communication DTCs against the FFCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Forward Facing Camera Module (FFCM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the EPS pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1601-00 ecu application software code 1 missing or corrupted\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1601-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU APPLICATION SOFTWARE CODE 1 MISSING OR CORRUPTED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module detects that its software has been corrupted or is missing.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS is disabled. No power steering assist.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC must be active for the results of this test to be valid. Check for a loose scan tool connection. Verify battery charger is installed and charge rate provides approximately 13.5 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on vehicle work order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read EPS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE. STANDARD PROCEDURE EPS VERIFICATION TEST</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">EPS VERIFICATION TEST</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove all test equipment.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Torque Sensor (Grey) harness connector is connected properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect all previously disconnected components and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Verify all accessories are turned off, the battery is fully charged and the charging system has a status of &quot;charged&quot;.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Verify that the ignition is on. With the scan tool, record and erase all Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) from all modules. Start the engine and allow it to run for two minutes and fully operate the system that was indicating the failure.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Turn the steering wheel from stop to stop, holding at each stop position for One second.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off and wait five minutes. Turn the ignition on and using the scan tool, read DTCs from all modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If there are no DTCs present after turning ignition on, road test the vehicle while turning the steering wheel from stop to stop for at least five minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Again, with the scan tool read DTCs. If any DTCs are present, refer to the DTC INDEX in the applicable section for the Diagnostic procedure and troubleshoot the new or recurring symptom.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>If there are no DTCs present and the customer&#x27;s concern can no longer be duplicated, the repair is complete.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any DTCs present or is the original concern still present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910299</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
